      "id": "m1",
      "title": "Implement parseCsv and toObjects in src/csv.js",
      "status": "done",
      "plan": "Implement the two exported functions in src/csv.js according to the spec, and add a node:test suite at test/csv.test.js.\n\n## parseCsv(text)\n- Return an array of rows; each row an array of strings.\n- Comma separates fields; \n or \r\n ends a line.\n- A field wrapped in double quotes may contain commas and line breaks; \"\" inside a quoted field is one double quote.\n- A final line break does not add an empty row; empty text returns [].\n\n## toObjects(rows)\n- First row is the header; return one object per remaining row keyed by header.\n- A short row gets empty strings for missing columns.\n\n## Tests\n- test/csv.test.js uses node:test and node:assert, covering: empty text, plain rows, CRLF, quoted commas, embedded newlines, escaped quotes, trailing newline, toObjects header mapping and short rows.\n- Run npm test (node --test).",
      "preview": null,
      "dispatch": null,
